{
  "thesis": "Position FlytBase as the operational standard for the Novandino Litio joint venture to manage the 70% production increase and US$3B 'Salar Futuro' expansion without increasing human risk or contractor headcount. By automating 24/7 inspections across the Atacama's remote lithium and iodine infrastructure, SQM can maintain its low-cost producer status while directly addressing the Safety, Health and Environment Committee's mandate to remove personnel from hazardous desert conditions.",
